<title>SINGAPORE: OUE does not see better 1997 pretax.</title>
<headline>OUE does not see better 1997 pretax.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hotel-based Overseas Union Enterprise Ltd (OUE) said on Friday it did not see better pretax profits in 1997 compared to 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;The projected pretax profits for the company and the group in 1997 will not be better than those achieved last year,&quot; it said in a statement accompanying its first half results.</p>
<p>This was &quot;on account of higher interest charge on increased borrowings and the negative earnings from Hainan Mandarin anticipated in the second half year,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>OUE said first half net profits fell 4.3 percent to Singapore $13.6 million, against S$14.21 million previously.  </p>
